			"Message": "docs(Echo): Detail work-stealing architecture in Mermaid diagram\n\nReplace the abstract three-box architecture diagram with a granular breakdown of Echo's internal modules — Scheduler/, Queue/, Task/ — each referencing concrete Rust source files (SchedulerBuilder.rs, Scheduler.rs, Worker.rs, StealingQueue.rs, Task.rs, Priority.rs).\n\nThe revised diagram traces the full task lifecycle: Common defines ActionEffect and the Prioritized trait, Mountain dispatches via Track through ApplicationRunTime, Echo's SchedulerCore enqueues into the lock-free StealingQueue, and idle WorkerPool threads steal tasks before executing against Mountain's Environment providers. The nested subgraph layout and color-coded class definitions make the architecture scannable at a glance.\n\nThis aligns the README with the actual codebase structure now present under Documentation/Rust/.",
